# WGSN catwalk renditions and the snapshot that indexes them. This repository
# is public, so committing them would redistribute subscription imagery to
# anyone on github.com no matter what access control the site itself carries.
# They are built locally by `npm run catwalk` and deployed only to the
# access-controlled internal project by `npm run internal` - see
# docs/internal-deployment.md. The public build simply has no catwalk.json,
# and the tab hides itself when there is none.
public/catwalk/
public/data/catwalk.json

# Per-season WGSN fragments composed into public/data/catwalk.json, and the
# runway index built from the same source. Both carry WGSN's own metadata and
# original-image URLs for subscription content, so neither belongs in a public
# repository - the same rule as the renditions above.
data/catwalk/
data/wgsn-runway.json

# The weekly catwalk run's working files. catwalk-originals holds WGSN
# renditions downsized from the subscription originals, and the .log/.html
# outputs quote what was collected - none of it belongs in a public repository.
logs/catwalk-originals/
logs/*.log
logs/*.html

# WGSN collection: the code that talks to WGSN's own endpoints, the session
# helper, the weekly runner and its documentation. This repository is public
# and belongs to an organisation account; a public description of how to call
# a subscription service's private API is a liability even though it exposes
# no credential and no imagery. Collection only ever runs on the PC that holds
# config/wgsn-runway.local.json and a signed-in browser profile, so nothing is
# lost by keeping these out of the repository.
config/wgsn-runway.local.json
scripts/collect-catwalk-season.mjs
scripts/wgsn-login.mjs
scripts/update-catwalk.mjs
scripts/register-catwalk-task.ps1
tests/catwalk-collect.test.mjs
docs/wgsn-runway-automation.md

# The curation board's data: which brands this collection cannot verify, and
# why. That is our own QA state, not something to publish on a site anyone can
# open, so it is built locally and uploaded to the internal deployment only -
# the same route the catwalk renditions take. The board hides itself when the
# file is absent, so the public build simply has no board.
public/data/curation-summary.json
public-redirect/

# Internal WGSN Forecast and feed assets.
public/forecast/
public/data/forecast.json
data/wgsn-fashion/
logs/20261103/forecast-work/
public/data/catalog-index.json
public/data/catalog-brands/
public/data/research-brief.json
data/research-history.json
logs/20261103/brief-work/

